        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-24T08:48:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ok. I found the problem. There are several issues:\n1. With ciborium_io, when we send a vector of `N` bytes, the actual size is `2N + header size(12 bytes)`, because each item in the vector has a type Tag attached to it. So when we send a vector of 506 bytes, the actual size is 506*2+12\u003d1024 bytes.\n2. With long messages (\u003e800 bytes), the tests become flaky when running many times. It\u0027s hard to reproduce this, I think it might be related to resource limitation in rialto when the host sends lots of small messages of 1 byte. This is resolved when we change to `BufWriter` in host and send the messages by big chunks.\n3. A credit update is missing in the vsock connection manager\u0027s `recv()`. Once this is fixed and we use buffer writer, we can send messages longer than its max buffer 1024 bytes without problem. I\u0027ll send a PR in the upstream repo to fix it.",
      "parentUuid": "b25efa6f_cb61ca07",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 139,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 139,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "ac813f7330fe293b6f21fa4eaa163e12fea4c515",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
